cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "Structure-Based Screening of the AlphaFold Human Proteome for Candidate Copper-Binding Proteins"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Adebowale"
    given-names: "Damilare Desmond"
    affiliation: "Purdue University"

repository-code: "https://github.com/damilareadebowale/Copper"
url: "https://github.com/damilareadebowale/Copper"

version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-08-14

doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22349882"

license: MIT

abstract: >-
  This software provides a Python workflow for structure-based screening of
  AlphaFold-predicted human protein models for cysteine-pair motifs consistent
  with candidate copper coordination. The workflow identifies cysteine sulfur
  atoms, filters cysteine pairs by sulfur-to-sulfur distance, and uses
  MSMS-derived solvent-excluded surfaces to calculate individual-residue and
  motif-center depth as measures of structural accessibility. A benchmark set
  of established human copper-handling proteins is tracked through the
  workflow to assess filter behavior. The resulting CSV outputs support
  transparent candidate prioritization and downstream experimental assessment.
  Structural matches generated by the workflow are hypotheses and do not by
  themselves establish copper binding or copper-chaperone activity.

keywords:
  - "structural bioinformatics"
  - "AlphaFold"
  - "copper-binding proteins"
  - "metalloproteins"
  - "cysteine geometry"
  - "molecular surface analysis"
  - "Python"
